      "message": "The Binder driver does it this way because some of the structs contain padding. If your uapi has no padding, then there\u0027s a simpler way to do it. (And really it shouldn\u0027t have padding.)\n\nSpecifically, you can implement `FromBytes`/`AsBytes` directly for the uapi types and use the raw uapi types everywhere instead of these wrappers.\n\nOn this branch, you may need to place the `impl FromBytes` and `impl AsBytes` block to make that work inside the `kernel` branch. You can place them in the same file as where the traits are declared.",
